        "id": "deep-dive",
        "type": "content",
        "title": "Why Asian Businesses Need AI Legal Tools Specifically",
        "content": "Asia presents unique legal challenges that AI tools are only beginning to address. **Common law vs civil law:** Singapore, Malaysia, Hong Kong, and India follow English common law, while Thailand, Vietnam, Indonesia, China, Japan, and Korea are civil law jurisdictions. An NDA template designed for common law might miss requirements under Thailand's Civil and Commercial Code. **Multi-language contracts:** A Malaysian business might have contracts in English, Malay, and Chinese \u2014 most AI tools only parse English well. **Currency and jurisdiction clauses:** SE Asian contracts often reference SGD, MYR, or THB with specific jurisdiction clauses. Tools like Spellbook can flag missing currency conversion terms, which are crucial when a Singapore supplier invoices in SGD but an Indonesian buyer pays in IDR. **Local regulations matter:** Data privacy laws vary dramatically \u2014 Singapore's PDPA, Thailand's PDPA, Malaysia's PDPA, and Indonesia's UU PDP are all different. AI tools are slowly adding awareness of these variations, but as of 2026, most still default to US/EU frameworks."
