        "id": "regional-guide",
        "type": "content",
        "title": "Regional Setup Guide for Asian Sellers & Manufacturers",
        "content": "**Singapore e-commerce seller:** Stack = Zoho Inventory ($19/mo) + Shopee/Lazada plug-ins + Ninja Van/J&T Express integration. AI handles demand forecasting for CNY, 11.11, and 12.12. Total cost: $19-39/mo. **Malaysian small manufacturer:** Katana ($99/mo) for production planning + inFlow for raw material inventory. If you make-to-order (batik, furniture, food products), Katana's AI production scheduling is worth the premium. **Thai restaurant group / F&B:** inFlow Inventory ($89/mo) with batch tracking for perishable ingredients + AI reorder points based on daily sales data from LINE MAN or GrabFood. **Indonesia e-commerce (TikTok Shop):** Google Sheets + Julius AI ($20/mo) for bootstrapping. Upgrade to Zoho Inventory when you hit 100+ orders/month. Most Indonesian sellers start on TikTok Shop and expand to Shopee/Tokopedia later. **Vietnam manufacturer:** Katana for BOM and production scheduling. Most Vietnamese factories are B2B/OEM, so manufacturing-focused tools work better than retail inventory tools."
