        "content": "SEO in Asia is fundamentally different from SEO in the West. Google dominates in Singapore, Malaysia, and the Philippines, but Baidu holds 60%+ search share in China, Naver rules South Korea, Yahoo Japan is still relevant in Japan, and C\u1ed1c C\u1ed1c has a meaningful share in Vietnam. Your keywords are different (people search in local languages), your competition is different (Shopee product pages rank for everything), and your content strategy must be different (mobile-first, short-form, local platform integration). AI-powered SEO tools have evolved to handle these realities. We tested Semrush AI, Surfer SEO, Neuron Writer, RankIQ, and more against Asia-specific SEO challenges: multi-language keyword research, Baidu optimization, local search intent analysis, and content generation for diverse markets."
